      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "VRChat management seemingly only lets their devs work on bug fixes when a \"major rework\" is involved so this post is to try help argue for that.\nTo start it off a small example of Network IK jitter.\nhttps://user-images.githubusercontent.com/104001796/164468165-bcc211b1-a9a5-4429-bbce-ff79ba20a231.mp4\nBones flipping from low update rate and/or incorrectly applied interpolation. \nhttps://user-images.githubusercontent.com/104001796/164467306-f6da9735-d324-47b0-9a75-10af54b4983e.mp4\nIndex root motion bug that has been fixed and regressed countless times.\nhttps://user-images.githubusercontent.com/104001796/164468566-35b82763-110e-4c23-920e-910ee9f6cf6d.mp4\nUnnecessarily low IK update rate in general.\nhttps://user-images.githubusercontent.com/104001796/164469092-99fc29f5-f5bd-4c17-bcde-7f55caac7f9e.mp4\nAnd because radial floats are sent with IK sync, radial menu opens on wrong value remotely.\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/avatar-30/p/bug-float-on-a-radial-open-on-wrong-value-remotely",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
